{% decision_card number="ADR-0008" status="approved" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

Claude and Codex can perform overlapping work, while company responsibility must remain clear.

## Decision drivers

- One deliverable owner
- Provider replacement
- Capacity fallback
- Measured affinity

## Options considered

- Claude architecture/Codex coding permanently
- Unstructured free-for-all
- Stable roles with broker assignment

## Decision

Define role contracts independently of providers. Assign Claude or Codex per work unit using policy, capability, preference, health, capacity, context, and affinity.

## Positive consequences

- No permanent model department
- Fallback preserves business meaning

## Negative consequences

- Routing policy needs evidence and tuning

## Risks

- Affinity may harden into unsupported stereotype

## Follow-up work

- Measure quality by task category
- Keep Claude-first configurable

## Supersedes or superseded by

New decision; superseded by: none.

